35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I've found that our previous arrangements had extremes. One year we had no privacy in a shared house, and last year we were so separate we barely saw each other. We need a balance.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've learned that all-in rates can be unfair to light eaters, and separate bookings often lead to uneven costs. A single bill for a whole building seems much fairer for everyone involved.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the island houses only have one bathroom and the water might be cold. Also, the inns have very strict mealtimes and we would all sleep in one room on futons.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Regarding travel, the train to the spa valley is quite fast. However, the ferry for the island takes up two full days of our trip, and the valley's bus service is limited.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've looked at the costs. The island houses are very affordable at 5,400 yen per night, while the valley inn is around 17,000 yen including meals. City beds are the most unpredictable, ranging from 12,000 to 20,000 yen.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Minato, the idea of everyone in one room on futons sounds like it might be too crowded, especially given what I found about the lack of privacy in shared houses. We should be careful.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, thank you for the pricing. It seems the island is the most economical, but @Shizue's point about a single bill for a whole building makes it very appealing for fairness.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mizuki, I agree. Sleeping in one room and having strict mealtimes makes me a bit nervous. I think having my own space or more flexibility would help me sleep better and feel more relaxed.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the island's low cost is tempting, but the travel time is a major drawback. Losing two days to the ferry seems excessive. The spa valley is much more accessible, though the bus limits our movement.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, I agree that the travel time is a concern. However, the city option seems the most expensive and unpredictable. I'd prefer something where we know the total cost upfront rather than paying in installments.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we want to avoid the extremes of being too crowded or too distant, the city might be too separate, and the island house too cramped. Perhaps the spa town is a middle ground?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"The spa town sounds lovely, but we must consider the cost. If the inn is a fixed rate, it might be simpler, though we should ensure it is fair for everyone.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried about the spa town too. If we all sleep in one room on futons and have to eat at exact times, I might feel trapped. I'd prefer a place with more space.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I understand. If the spa town feels too restrictive, the city offers the most freedom and the shortest travel time, which is a huge plus for me. However, we must weigh that against the cost.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, the city's flexibility is great, but the price range is worrying. If we choose the city, how will we handle the costs to ensure no one is surprised by the final bill?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we are torn between flexibility and predictability. The city offers the most personal space and ease of travel, but the costs are vague. The spa town is efficient but potentially too restrictive for Minato.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Perhaps we can find a way to make the costs predictable even in the city? I simply wish for an arrangement where no one feels they have paid more than their fair share.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think the city sounds the most relaxing for me because of the separate rooms and no strict schedule. I don't want to be stressed about the bathroom or mealtimes this year.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Minato. The city's accessibility and the lack of a rigid schedule would make the trip far more restful. If we can solve the cost uncertainty, it seems the most balanced choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I understand the appeal of the city for your comfort and time, but the price range is quite wide. If we can agree on a budget cap beforehand, I would be more comfortable with that option.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
